---
import BekkerJump from '../components/BekkerJump.svelte';
import '../styles/global.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Texts &amp; Licences — Nicomachean Ethics</title>
  <link rel="icon" href={`${base}/favicon.svg`} type="image/svg+xml" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cardo:ital@0;1&family=EB+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    .attr-body {
      max-width: 680px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 2rem 1rem 4rem;
      font-family: var(--font-english);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.75;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-ui);
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--accent);
      margin: 2rem 0 0.4rem;
      letter-spacing: .02em;
    }
    h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 1rem; }
    p { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
    a { color: var(--accent); }
    .licence-badge {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: var(--font-ui);
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: .06em;
      background: var(--border);
      border-radius: 3px;
      padding: 0.1em 0.5em;
      margin-left: 0.4em;
      vertical-align: middle;
      color: var(--text-mid);
    }
    .licence-badge.cc { background: #e8f4e8; color: #2a6a2a; }
    .licence-badge.pd { background: #e8eef4; color: #2a4a6a; }
    .licence-badge.mit { background: #f4f0e8; color: #6a4a2a; }
    blockquote {
      border-left: 3px solid var(--border);
      margin: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem 1rem;
      padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1rem;
      color: var(--text-mid);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
    .greek { font-family: var(--font-greek); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1><a href={`${base}/`} style="text-decoration:none;color:inherit">Nicomachean Ethics</a></h1>
    <BekkerJump client:load />
    <nav class="book-nav" aria-label="Navigation">
      {Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, i) => (
        <a href={`${base}/book/${i + 1}`}>
          {['I','II','III','IV','V','VI','VII','VIII','IX','X'][i]}
        </a>
      ))}
      <a href={`${base}/search`} class="search-link">Search</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <div class="attr-body">
    <h2>Texts &amp; Licences</h2>
    <p>
      This reader presents three bodies of text compiled from public-domain
      editions and openly licensed reference works. Their sources and licence
      terms are listed below.
    </p>

    <h2>
      Greek Lexicon (LSJ)
      <span class="licence-badge cc">CC BY-SA 3.0</span>
    </h2>
    <p>
      The word popups and lemma entries are drawn from the
      <em>Greek–English Lexicon</em> of Henry George Liddell and Robert Scott,
      revised by Sir Henry Stuart Jones with the assistance of Roderick McKenzie
      (Oxford: Clarendon Press, 9th ed. 1940; supplement 1996).
    </p>
    <p>
      The machine-readable edition used here is the XML transcription prepared
      by the <a href="https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/">Perseus Digital Library</a>
      at Tufts University and is made available under a
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/us/">
        Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 United States</a> licence.
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      Liddell, Henry George, and Robert Scott.
      <em>A Greek-English Lexicon.</em>
      Revised and augmented by Henry Stuart Jones.
      Oxford: Clarendon Press, 1940.
      Machine-readable version: Perseus Digital Library,
      Trustees of Tufts University.
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/us/">CC BY-SA 3.0 US</a>.
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      The CC BY-SA licence requires that any derivative work be distributed
      under the same terms. This application's lexical data is a subset and
      derivative of that work; users who redistribute it must carry this
      attribution notice and the same CC BY-SA licence.
    </p>

    <h2>
      English Translations
      <span class="licence-badge pd">Public Domain</span>
    </h2>
    <p>
      The reader offers two English translations, chosen from the
      <em>Translation</em> menu.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>H. Rackham.</strong>
      The Loeb Classical Library translation of the
      <span class="greek">Ἠθικὰ Νικομάχεια</span>, first published in the
      United States in 1926 and in the public domain. It is anchored to the
      Bekker line numbers, which appear in the gutter beside it.
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      Aristotle. <em>Nicomachean Ethics.</em>
      Translated by H. Rackham.
      Loeb Classical Library 73.
      Cambridge, MA: Harvard University Press, 1926.
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      The TEI XML edition used as the source is hosted by the
      <a href="https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/">Perseus Digital Library</a>
      (canonical-greekLit repository, file
      <code>tlg0086.tlg010.perseus-eng2.xml</code>).
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>W. D. Ross.</strong>
      The Oxford translation, first published in 1908 and revised in
      <em>The Works of Aristotle Translated into English</em> (vol. IX,
      Oxford: Clarendon Press, 1925); in the public domain in the United States.
      Ross is presented chapter by chapter (it carries no Bekker line numbers of
      its own).
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      Aristotle. <em>Nicomachean Ethics.</em>
      Translated by W. D. Ross. In <em>The Works of Aristotle Translated into
      English</em>, vol. IX. Oxford: Clarendon Press, 1925.
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      The text is transcribed from the
      <a href="https://classics.mit.edu/Aristotle/nicomachaen.html">MIT
      Internet Classics Archive</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>
      Greek Text
      <span class="licence-badge pd">Public Domain</span>
    </h2>
    <p>
      The Greek presented here is the ancient text of Aristotle's own words — a
      public-domain work — in the edition of Ingram Bywater, <strong>without</strong>
      the critical apparatus, editorial notes, or commentary:
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      Aristotle. <span class="greek">Ἀριστοτέλους Ἠθικὰ Νικομάχεια.</span>
      Edited by Ingram Bywater.
      Oxford: Clarendon Press (Oxford Classical Texts), 1894.
      Reprinted 1962.
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      The electronic text was generated from the Thesaurus Linguae Graecae (TLG)
      digitisation via the <a href="https://d.iogen.es/">Diogenes</a> export tool.
      The TLG corpus is separately licensed from the
      <a href="https://stephanus.tlg.uci.edu/">University of California, Irvine</a>.
      Only the bare Greek text — the public-domain words of Aristotle — is
      included here; none of the TLG's apparatus, notes, or other database
      content is reproduced.
    </p>

    <h2>
      Morphological Data
      <span class="licence-badge pd">Open</span>
    </h2>
    <p>
      Morphological analyses (lemma, gloss, grammatical parse) are produced
      by the Morpheus morphological analyser as distributed with
      <a href="https://d.iogen.es/">Diogenes</a>.
      See the Diogenes and Perseus project pages for applicable terms.
    </p>

    <h2>
      Application Code
      <span class="licence-badge mit">MIT</span>
    </h2>
    <p>
      The pipeline and web application source code (Python and TypeScript/Svelte)
      are released under the
      <a href="https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT">MIT Licence</a>.
      Data files derived from CC BY-SA sources are excluded from this grant
      and remain subject to CC BY-SA.
    </p>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
